# One check per line, as: label|command
# The command runs from the repository root through `sh -c`, and the gate stops at the first one that fails. Order them from the
# quickest to the slowest. Layers add their own lines (format, static analysis, tests); keep a line only if the check exists.
# Example: Tests|npm test
Rules and skills registered|scripts/check-registry.sh
Gate self-test|scripts/selftest.sh

Dependency audit (PHP)|composer audit --locked --no-interaction
Dependency audit (JavaScript)|npm audit --omit=dev
.env has every variable of .env.example|php artisan env:check
Pint (code style)|vendor/bin/pint --test --format agent
PHPStan (types)|vendor/bin/phpstan analyse --memory-limit=1G --no-progress
Build (Vite manifest and Wayfinder files)|npm run build
Tests|php artisan test --compact

Front-end standards|node scripts/check-standards.mjs
Front-end checks (format, lint, tests)|npm run check
Copied code|npx jscpd
Types|npm run types:check
